---
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Environmental Performance Simulation — Sayali Lamne</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Raleway:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

    body {
      font-family: 'Raleway', sans-serif;
      background: #ffffff;
      color: #111111;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* ── Nav ── */
    .nav { padding: 16px 6%; }
    .back {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: #db634c;
      text-decoration: none;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .back:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* ── Hero image ── */
    .hero-image {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      overflow: visible;
    }
    .hero-image img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }
    .hero-stack {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .hero-clip {
      width: 72%;
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .hero-clip--top {
      max-height: 480px;
    }
    .hero-clip--top img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      margin-top: -90px;
    }
    .hero-clip--bottom {
      max-height: 360px;
      margin-top: -80px;
    }
    .hero-clip--bottom img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      margin-top: -230px;
    }
    .hero-image__num {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: -16px;
      left: 5%;
      font-size: clamp(80px, 14vw, 160px);
      font-weight: 700;
      color: rgba(0,0,0,0.07);
      line-height: 1;
      user-select: none;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    /* ── Content ── */
    .content {
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 1.7% 100px;
    }

    .project-title {
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 48px);
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.3px;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }
    .project-tag {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #db634c;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    }
    .divider {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid #e8e8e8;
      margin: 28px 0;
    }
    .meta {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.9;
      color: #111;
      margin-bottom: 36px;
    }
    .body-text p {
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 300;
      line-height: 1.85;
      color: #333;
      text-align: justify;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .body-text p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    /* ── Section heading ── */
    .section-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #db634c;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }

    /* ── Full-width single image ── */
    .full-img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .img-caption {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: #888;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    /* ── Image grid 2-col ── */
    .grid-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .grid-2 img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }

    /* ── Image grid 3-col ── */
    .grid-3 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .grid-3 img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }

    /* ── Image grid 4-col ── */
    .grid-4 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .grid-4 img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }

    /* ── Solar Radiation section ── */
    .solar-heading {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #db634c;
      margin-top: 64px;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .solar-two-col {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0 48px;
    }
    .solar-col-heading {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #db634c;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e8e8e8;
      padding-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .solar-sub-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #111;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .sed-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .sed-row-3 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 6px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .sed-row-4 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 6px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .sed-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
    .sed-item img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
    .sed-caption {
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: #555;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
    .sed-summary {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: #444;
      line-height: 1.7;
      text-align: justify;
      margin-top: 16px;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    .img-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
    .img-item img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
    .img-item-caption {
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: #555;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    /* ── Thermal radiation cards ── */
    .thermal-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 24px 32px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .thermal-card img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .thermal-card-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: #555;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    /* ── Thermal Radiation two-col ── */
    .thermal-two-col {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0 48px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .thermal-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    .thermal-sub-label {
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #db634c;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .thermal-body {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 300;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #333;
      text-align: justify;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .pvmd-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 12px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
    .pvmd-table th, .pvmd-table td {
      border: 1px solid #d0d0d0;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .pvmd-table th {
      font-weight: 600;
      background: #f7f7f7;
      color: #111;
    }
    .pvmd-table td { font-weight: 300; color: #333; }

    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .thermal-two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .study-two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .thermal-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .grid-3, .grid-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <nav class="nav">
    <a class="back" href="/projects/building-performance">← Back to Building Performance</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="hero-image">
    <div class="hero-stack">
      <div class="hero-clip hero-clip--top">
        <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/Furniture Model.png" alt="Furniture model — open office and conference room" />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-clip hero-clip--bottom">
        <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/Glazing Location.png" alt="Glazing location — isometric view" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <span class="hero-image__num">02</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Content -->
  <div class="content">

    <h1 class="project-title">Environmental Performance Simulation</h1>
    <span class="project-tag">Energy Modeling</span>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <div class="meta">
      <div>Instructor: Omer T. Karaguzel</div>
      <div>Master in Sustainable Design &nbsp;|&nbsp; Carnegie Mellon University, PA &nbsp;|&nbsp; 2023</div>
      <div>Tools: Rhino, Grasshopper, Climate Studio &amp; Ladybug Plugin</div>
      <div>Type of Work: Team Work</div>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <div class="body-text">
      <p>
        The Environmental Performance Simulation (EPS) course provides an in-depth exploration of building
        energy modeling, thermal analysis, and environmental simulation methods used in sustainable design.
        Using parametric tools within Rhino and Grasshopper, the course equips students with computational
        methods to evaluate and optimize building performance across multiple environmental criteria.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project investigates Solar Radiation, Thermal Radiation, and Visible Radiation simulations to
        understand the effects of surface orientation, glazing location, and building massing on occupant
        comfort and energy consumption. Parametric studies using Climate Studio and the Ladybug Plugin were
        conducted across annual, summer, and winter conditions to identify optimal design strategies.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ── A. Solar Radiation Studies ── -->
    <h2 class="solar-heading">A. Solar Radiation Studies</h2>

    <!-- Bar charts side by side -->
    <div style="margin-top:32px;">
      <img class="full-img" src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/Two Charts.png"
           alt="Comparison of Total SED on different surfaces and orientations" />
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:0 48px; margin-top:6px;">
        <p class="img-caption" style="text-align:center; font-style:italic;">Comparison of Total SED on different surfaces</p>
        <p class="img-caption" style="text-align:center; font-style:italic;">Comparison of Total SED with different building orientations</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary paragraphs -->
    <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:0 48px; margin-top:20px; margin-bottom:40px;">
      <p class="sed-summary">
        Above comparison suggests roof followed by South facade received the most solar radiation.
        Based on SED analysis we can propose the passive design strategies to reduce, eliminate,
        or utilize the solar gain.
      </p>
      <p class="sed-summary">
        Above comparison suggests N-90 is giving lowest incident solar radiation. This study helps
        understand the optimum orientation to reduce solar gain, thus heating &amp; cooling loads
        for the building.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ── B. Thermal Radiation Studies ── -->
    <h2 class="solar-heading" style="margin-top:64px;">B. Thermal Radiation Studies</h2>

    <div class="thermal-two-col">

      <!-- ══ LEFT COLUMN ══ -->
      <div class="thermal-col">

        <!-- Hourly temperature chart -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Graph.png" alt="Open Office Extreme Cold Week Hourly Temperature" />
        </div>

        <p class="thermal-sub-label">Hourly Temperature Analysis</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          The graph shows that indoor zone temp. is higher compared to site temp. due to internal
          loads &amp; lag in heat transfer caused by building envelope in the absence of HVAC system.
        </p>

        <!-- Grasshopper spatial comfort setup -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin: 20px 0;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/4b-Spatial Thermal Comfort ANalysis.png" alt="Run Spatial Comfort — Grasshopper setup" />
        </div>

        <!-- Coldest/Hottest day spatial comfort -->
        <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:8px;">
          <div class="img-item">
            <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Spatial comfort-12.png" alt="Coldest day spatial comfort" />
            <span class="img-item-caption" style="font-style:italic;">1. Coldest day (Jan 08)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="img-item">
            <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/spatial comfort -21.png" alt="Hottest day spatial comfort" />
            <span class="img-item-caption" style="font-style:italic;">2. Hottest day (April 29)</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- PMV/PPD table -->
        <table class="pvmd-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>HVAC Status</th>
              <th>Date</th>
              <th>Mean PMV</th>
              <th>Mean PPD</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>OFF</td><td>Jan 8th, 06H</td><td>1.53</td><td>52.4%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ON</td><td>Jan 8th, 06H</td><td>1.66</td><td>58.3%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>OFF</td><td>Apr 29th, 12H</td><td>2.06</td><td>74.5%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ON</td><td>Apr 29th, 12H</td><td>2.21</td><td>85.1%</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-top:6px;">Summary of PMV &amp; PPD for Open Office</p>

        <p class="thermal-sub-label" style="margin-top:24px;">Spatial Thermal Comfort Analysis</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          The simulation output show distribution of Mean Radiant Temperature throughout the zone for open
          office without HVAC. The results from MRT, PMV, &amp; PPD suggest that on the coldest day (refer 1)
          employees working near the glazing may experience a cooler environment compared to the north side,
          whereas on the hottest (refer 2) employees seating near windows felt warmer compared to rest of the room.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ══ RIGHT COLUMN ══ -->
      <div class="thermal-col">

        <!-- Heat Loss chart -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Hourly heat loss.png" alt="Open Office Heat Loss — January 21" />
        </div>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:24px;">Heat Loss for the Open Office on January 21</p>

        <!-- Heat Gain chart -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/hourly heat gain.png" alt="Open Office Heat Gain — July 21" />
        </div>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:24px;">Heat Gain for the Open Office on July 21</p>

        <p class="thermal-sub-label">Hourly Temperature Analysis</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          The results of the heat loss &amp; heat gain simulation have a direct relationship with the
          occupancy of the building. Zone infiltration total heat gain energy and zone windows total
          transmitted solar radiation energy is due presence of glazing.
        </p>

        <!-- Picture1_1 overview -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin-top:24px;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Picture1_1.png" alt="Thermal radiation study overview" />
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ── Second thermal block ── -->
    <div class="thermal-two-col" style="margin-top:56px;">

      <!-- ══ LEFT ══ -->
      <div class="thermal-col">

        <!-- Monthly energy consumption charts -->
        <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:8px;">
          <div class="img-item">
            <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Open office.png" alt="Open Office Heating & Cooling Energy Consumption" />
            <span class="img-item-caption" style="font-style:italic;">Open Office</span>
          </div>
          <div class="img-item">
            <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/conference room.png" alt="Conference Heating & Cooling Energy Consumption" />
            <span class="img-item-caption" style="font-style:italic;">Closed Conference Room</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="thermal-sub-label">Heating and Cooling Energy Consumption Analysis</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          The open office space uses more energy to cool the space than heat the space during all months
          of the year. The conference room uses less energy to heat and cool the space due to lack of glazing.
        </p>

        <!-- Load CS Energy Results Grasshopper diagram -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin: 20px 0;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Picture1_1.png" alt="Load CS Energy Results — Grasshopper setup" />
        </div>

        <!-- Site EUI / Carbon / Cost table -->
        <table class="pvmd-table" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Site EUI<br/>(kWh/m2/yr)</th>
              <th>Carbon Emissions<br/>(kgCO2/m2/yr)</th>
              <th>Energy Cost<br/>($/m2/yr)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>84.94</td><td>44.85</td><td>10.67</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="thermal-sub-label" style="margin-top:20px;">Whole-Building Environmental Performance Analysis</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          The "Load CS Energy Results" component is used to calculate the three metrics Whole Building
          EUI, Carbon Emissions, and Operational Costs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ══ RIGHT ══ -->
      <div class="thermal-col">

        <!-- Heat Pump systems comparison table -->
        <table class="pvmd-table" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Properties</th>
              <th>Base case</th>
              <th style="color:#db634c;">HVAC -1</th>
              <th style="color:#db634c;">HVAC -2</th>
              <th style="color:#db634c;">HVAC -3</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>System</td>
              <td>Heat Pump</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">Air-Source Heat Pumps</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">Water Source Heat Pump</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">Ground Source Heat Pump</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Heating System COP</td>
              <td>3.419</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">3.81</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">4</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">5</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Cooling System COP</td>
              <td>2.967</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">3.22</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">3.66</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">4.21</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Heat Recovery Ventilator (HRV)</td>
              <td>OFF Type: Sensible</td>
              <td>OFF Type: Sensible</td>
              <td>OFF Type: Sensible</td>
              <td>OFF Type: Sensible</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:20px;">Variations of Heat Pump systems used compared to baseline system</p>

        <!-- HVAC Performances bar chart -->
        <div class="img-item" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <img src="/3. Environmnetal Performance Analysis/B. Thermal Radiation Studies/Graph.png" alt="Performances of HVAC Systems" />
        </div>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:20px;">Comparison of overall building performance for proposed iterations in HVAC systems with the baseline</p>

        <!-- Performance metrics table -->
        <table class="pvmd-table" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Performance</th>
              <th>Base case</th>
              <th>HVAC -1</th>
              <th>HVAC -2</th>
              <th style="color:#db634c;">HVAC -3</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Site EUI (kWh/m2/yr)</td>
              <td>84.94</td><td>83.51</td><td>81.97</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">79.9</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>CO2 Emission (kgCO2/m2/yr)</td>
              <td>44.85</td><td>44.09</td><td>43.28</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">42.19</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Energy Cost ($/m2/yr)</td>
              <td>10.67</td><td>10.48</td><td>10.29</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">10.03</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Comparison of Results</td>
              <td>—</td><td>-1.60%</td><td>-3.50%</td>
              <td style="color:#db634c;">-5.93%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="img-caption" style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:20px;">Results suggests GSHP is the most suitable system for the building</p>

        <p class="thermal-body" style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:4px;">Design Iterations:</p>
        <p class="thermal-sub-label" style="margin-top:0;">Changes in Heating-Cooling Mechanical System Types</p>
        <p class="thermal-body">
          To increase the efficiency of the mechanical system &amp; reduce EUI without compromising with
          occupant's thermal comfort we opted for three different 'Heat Pump Systems' options by increasing
          their COPs &amp; analyzed the 'Overall Building Performance'.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</body>
</html>
